AB  - With the rapid development in the areas such as automobile, aerospace, semiconductor, and chemical industry as well as the continuous integration and the miniaturization of microelectronic devices, the importance of thermal management has been significantly increased. To meet some requirements of thermal management, there is an urgent need to develop compact, lightweight, and highly-efficient heat exchangers. Compared with conventional manufacturing technologies, additive manufacturing technology offers an automated and innovative way to fabricate heat exchangers tailored to specific requirements. This study presents a comprehensive and critical review of state-of-the-art research on the applications of additive manufacturing in thermal management, including diverse design methodologies, material alternations, numerical analysis methods, processing methods, thermophysical properties, heat transfer and hydrodynamic performance, challenges in preparation of heat exchangers, and potential applications. Furthermore, some limitations to cost-effectiveness and technological challenges to the development of thermal management systems are discussed in detail, and the roles of artificial intelligence in structural optimization and additive manufacturing processes are reviewed. This is of great benefit to thermal management’s performance, sustainable development as well as cost savings.
